<%#
  Technology & skills — Depth Charge restyle (Task 8). The old icon grid
  (grouped by frontend/backend/frameworks/tools, each icon a link) collapses
  into a flat row of mono "chip" tags carrying the same real tool list —
  Figma and Storybook.js included, since those are genuinely part of the
  stack even though the design mock's example chips omit them. Chips are
  plain spans, not links: a deliberate spec decision so this reads as a tag
  cloud rather than a link farm. Solid chips are tools I already use; the
  dashed .chip--learning chips mark what I'm currently picking up.
%>
<section id="tech-stack" class="sec justify-content-end"
         data-sec data-role="stack" data-ax="0.34" data-label="Tech Stack">
  <div class="section-inner" style="max-width: 600px;">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">◆ Technology & Skills</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mb-4">The tools I reach for.</h2>

    <p class="mono-label">What I know</p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
      <span class="chip">JavaScript</span>
      <span class="chip">HTML5</span>
      <span class="chip">CSS3</span>
      <span class="chip">Sass</span>
      <span class="chip">Bootstrap</span>
      <span class="chip">Ruby</span>
      <span class="chip">PostgreSQL</span>
      <span class="chip">RSpec</span>
      <span class="chip">Ruby on Rails</span>
      <span class="chip">GitHub</span>
      <span class="chip">Figma</span>
      <span class="chip">OpenAI API</span>
      <span class="chip">Storybook.js</span>
    </div>

    <p class="mono-label">Learning</p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span class="chip chip--learning">React</span>
      <span class="chip chip--learning">Vue.js</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
